&lt;h3 id=&quot;a-file-with-a-step-not-automated-yet&quot;&gt;A file with a step not automated yet&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;dk-gherkin&quot;&gt;&lt;h4 id=&quot;declare-a-consignment-to-customs&quot;&gt;Declare a consignment to customs&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;dk-gherkin__tags&quot;&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;@FR-004&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a shipper&lt;br&gt;
I want to declare my cargo to customs before it sails&lt;br&gt;
So that the consignment clears the border without being held&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every consignment that crosses a customs border needs a declaration lodged
before the sailing’s cut-off. The declared value sets the duty owed, and an
insured consignment names the marine policy that covers it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;2 rules · 3 scenarios · 3 example rows&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;dk-gherkin__results&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Results:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 undefined, 4 passed · as of &lt;time datetime=&quot;2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z&quot;&gt;2026-10-19&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h5 id=&quot;background-4&quot;&gt;Background&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;dk-gherkin__steps&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;dk-gherkin__kw&quot;&gt;Given&lt;/strong&gt; a booked consignment from Rotterdam to Felixstowe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;dk-gherkin__kw&quot;&gt;And&lt;/strong&gt; the customs cut-off is 24 hours before the sailing departs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;dk-gherkin__kw&quot;&gt;And&lt;/strong&gt; goods with a declared value under 150 EUR are relieved of duty&lt;/li&gt;
